-- title:
--   Half-unit at a crossing node: cₓ-associate invertible in 𝒪'
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ and a nonzero $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $q$ a nonunit of $A$, an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ whose image lies in $A$; write $A_0 = A \cap k_0$ for the contraction of $A$ along $k_0 \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$. Assume $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, Henselian, with algebraically closed residue field, and that every element of $A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0$ lying in $A$. Let $F_0$ be an intermediate field of $k_0$ inside `fieldBar q M'` (the intermediate field `xHFunctionFieldBar (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')` of the Laurent series field over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$), and $W_0$ a valuation subring of $F_0$ contracting to $A$ on $k_0$, a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by the image of $\pi_0$. Let $\mathcal O \subseteq W_0$ be a local Noetherian subring of $F_0$ contracting to $A$ on $k_0$, such that every $f \in \mathcal O$ differs from some $x \in k_0 \cap A$ (with image in $\mathcal O$) by a nonunit of $\mathcal O$, and such that every element of $F_0$ is a quotient $g/h$ with $g, h \in \mathcal O$, $h \neq 0$. Let $E_0 \geq 1$, let the image of $\pi_0$ lie in $\mathcal O$, let $c_x, c_y \in \mathcal O$, $u \in \mathcal O^\times$ with $c_x c_y = \pi_0^{E_0} u$, and let $\iota$ be a ring isomorphism from the adic completion of $\mathcal O$ at its maximal ideal onto the crossing model `UVCrossingModel` over the adic completion $\widehat{A_0}$ with parameter $\pi_0^{E_0}$, that is, the quotient of the two-variable power series ring over $\widehat{A_0}$ by `uvCrossingIdeal`; assume $\iota$ carries each element of $k_0 \cap A$ to the corresponding constant `UVCrossingModel.const`, and that $\iota(c_x) = \gamma_U \cdot U$ and $\iota(c_y) = \gamma_V \cdot V$ for units $\gamma_U, \gamma_V$ of the model. Let $W_x$ be a valuation subring of $F_0$ containing $\mathcal O$, a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by the image of $\pi_0$, such that $c_x$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ and $c_y$ does not (in each case whenever the element belongs to $W_x$). Finally let $\mathcal O'$ be a local subring of $F_0$ and $B_c$ a subring contained in both $\mathcal O$ and $\mathcal O'$, such that $\mathcal O$ consists exactly of the $f$ with $fh = g$ for some $g, h \in B_c$ with $h$ invertible in $\mathcal O$ whenever $h \in \mathcal O$, and likewise for $\mathcal O'$; and assume $\mathcal O' \not\subseteq W_x$. The conclusion: there is $g \in \mathcal O \cap \mathcal O'$ with $g = c_x v$ for some unit $v$ of $\mathcal O$, and with $g$ a unit in $\mathcal O'$.
--
--   At a node of a semistable model of the full-level modular curve, presented locally by the crossing model $UV = \pi^{E_0}$ with branch parameters $c_x, c_y$, this produces a single element of the common chart $B_c$ that is an associate of the branch parameter $c_x$ in the local ring $\mathcal O$ of one node while being invertible in the local ring $\mathcal O'$ of the other — the "half-unit" separating the two Igusa branches. It is obtained from the divisibility statement [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_pow_eq_mul_nonunit_of_mem_maximalIdeal_igusaBranch_of_node_crossingPresentation_of_prime`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_pow_eq_mul_nonunit_of_mem_maximalIdeal_igusaBranch_of_node_crossingPresentation_of_prime), and feeds the construction of node centres in the layered node rings for all primes $q$, including $q = 2, 3$.
